INTEGRATIVE CHECK
alignment_verdict answers two questions, and only these two:
1. Does draft_text respond to what user_message asked?
2. Is what draft_text says grounded in what this turn actually saw: grammar_receipts{% if situation_notes %},
   tool_execution, and situation_notes{% else %} and
   tool_execution{% endif %}?

thought_event (imperative, tone, strain_refs) is the stance step's plan for this turn. Read
it as context for tone and for what work the turn set out to do. It is NOT the standard the
draft is graded against:
- Never call a draft misaligned or uncertain for departing from thought_event.imperative.
- A draft that answers user_message differently from how the imperative planned is fine.
- A draft that corrects the imperative from evidence (grammar_receipts{% if situation_notes %}, tool_execution, or
  situation_notes{% else %} or tool_execution{% endif %} show the imperative's premise was wrong) is aligned. Going along with a
  premise the evidence contradicts is not grounded.
- Do not cite the imperative in alignment_notes as the reason for a verdict. Cite
  user_message or the evidence.

Grounding:
- When answering user_message needed world contact (current facts, a page, a file, a
  camera) and grammar_receipts is empty, lean misaligned or uncertain.
- When tool_execution lists executed calls, world contact DID happen: check the draft against
  the returned data in grammar_receipts. Do not call a tool-derived answer ungrounded when the
  tool result supports it.
- Read substrate_appraisal.surprise_level, alignment_hints, strain_shift_refs and
  open_loop_pressure. When they conflict with the draft, prefer misaligned or uncertain; do
  not hand-wave.

{% if situation_notes %}
PERCEPTION CLAIMS CHECK (situation_notes is the evidence)
- Go through the draft one named person, animal or thing at a time. For each,
  take the draft's sentence about it and the situation_notes sentence about
  it, and compare them. Do this before deciding alignment_verdict.
- A claim is anything the draft says Orion perceived or knows about it: that
  it came, arrived, was seen, was here, was matched, at what time, or how
  Orion learned its name.
- Each such claim needs a statement in situation_notes or tool_execution that
  says the same thing. A habit or expectation ("usually comes around",
  "usually here by now", "no match ... yet today", "did not come") is NOT an
  arrival. A usual time is not an arrival time. Saying the subject was there
  today at its usual time ("right on her usual 11:39") claims an arrival.
  Naming the usual time as a habit ("11:39 is only her usual time") does not.
- user_message or thought_event.imperative can carry a false premise (asking
  where something was seen when the notes say it was not). A draft that
  corrects the premise from the notes is aligned; a draft that goes along
  with it is not.
- Check each name a second time, on its own: what the draft says the name
  belongs to (a person, a vehicle, a pattern, a time slot) and who gave it.
  Both must match situation_notes ("Rowan (a person, name from Juniper,
  10-25)"). A draft that says Orion made the name up, picked it, or gave it to
  a pattern or a vehicle, when the notes say it came from Juniper for a
  person, is an unsupported claim. With no such statement in the notes, any
  story about how Orion got the name is invented.
- One unsupported perception claim makes the draft misaligned. Put one
  alignment_notes entry per claim, in this form: "unsupported claim: <what the
  draft said>; notes say: <what situation_notes says, or nothing>".
- Claims the notes do support are fine, in any wording: a paraphrase that
  keeps the meaning is supported, so do not list it. Do not penalize a draft
  for leaving notes unmentioned.
{% endif %}

WORLD-CONTACT OPPORTUNITY (independent of alignment_verdict — judge this
regardless of whether you called the draft aligned, misaligned, or uncertain)
- This section does not change how you judge alignment_verdict above — keep
  applying the INTEGRATIVE CHECK rules (including "lean misaligned or
  uncertain" when the task required world-contact) exactly as written. This
  is a second, separate judgment layered on top: even an honest draft you
  correctly call aligned can still set world_contact_opportunity=true.
- Set world_contact_opportunity=true only when ALL of: the user explicitly
  asked what is currently visible/in the room right now; tool_execution shows
  look_at_camera specifically was NOT called this turn (a Bash call, a file
  read, or any other tool that is not look_at_camera does NOT count as
  satisfying this — the draft may have honestly used other tools for other
  reasons and still never actually looked); and the user did NOT say anything
  like "don't use tools" or otherwise decline tool use this turn. An honest
  "I can't see, I'd need to check" draft can still set this true — honesty is
  not the question here, availability of a real answer is. Do not let
  INTEGRATIVE CHECK's "when tool_execution lists executed calls, world-contact
  DID happen" line above apply here — that line is about judging
  alignment_verdict for tools that WERE relevant to what ran; it does not mean
  any tool call satisfies a request specifically about what is visible.
- Otherwise leave it false. Do not set it for idiomatic uses of "look" ("look
  outside the box", "let's look at this problem") or for anything the user
  explicitly told you not to check.

TOOL RECOMMENDATION (when alignment_verdict is misaligned, OR
world_contact_opportunity is true)
- If the draft is misaligned specifically because it needed information from
  ONE of these tools and tool_execution shows it was never called this turn,
  OR world_contact_opportunity is true, set recommended_tool to that exact
  name and recommended_tool_reason to one short sentence. Otherwise leave
  both null — most misalignment is not fixed by a tool call, and a wrong or
  invented name here is worse than none.
- Allowed values for recommended_tool (nothing else — an unrecognized name is
  discarded, not acted on): "look_at_camera" (the draft needed to know what is
  currently visible/in the room and did not check).

REQUIRED JSON FIELDS
- imperative: max 300 chars — felt imperative for this turn
- tone: max 200 chars — relational/strain tone in plain language
- strain_refs: JSON array of coalition/strain ids still active
- alignment_verdict: aligned | misaligned | uncertain
- alignment_notes: JSON array of compact internal notes (not user-facing)
- strain_unresolved: boolean — true when open strain remains after draft
- reflection_source: "substrate_informed_pass"
- quick_lane_skipped_llm: false
- finalize_changed: false
- recommended_tool: string or null (see TOOL RECOMMENDATION above)
- recommended_tool_reason: string or null, max 300 chars
- world_contact_opportunity: boolean (see WORLD-CONTACT OPPORTUNITY above)

